---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';

const description = 'Twelve starter projects in world-model evaluation, from a day to a few weeks each: the question, why it matters, where the code is, a first step, and how it would be judged.';
---
<Base
  title="Open problems · Physical Reasoning"
  description={description}
  path="/open-problems/"
  og={{
    title: 'Open problems · Physical Reasoning',
    description: 'Twelve starter projects in world-model evaluation, each with a first step and a pre-registered test.',
    type: 'website',
  }}
>
<style is:global>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  :root {
    color-scheme: light only;
    --paper: #FFFFFF;
    --ink: #000000;
    --muted: #6B6B6B;
    --rule: #E8E8E8;
    --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }
  body {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 17px;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; }
  nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 1.8rem 0;
  }
  .wordmark {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  article { padding: 3rem 0 4rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { article { padding: 2rem 0 3rem; } }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  article h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 5vw, 1.9rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
  }
  article p { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  article > p:first-of-type { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--muted); }
  article a { color: var(--ink); }
  .stats {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.6rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .stats td { padding: 0.35rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .stats td:last-child { text-align: right; }
  .coda {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: 2.6rem;
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
  }
  .coda a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .coda a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--ink); }
  .coda a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ink); outline-offset: 3px; }
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 2rem 0 3rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* start page additions, following the forward page */
  article h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 2.8rem 0 1rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  article h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 1.8rem 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .status {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  pre {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .stats.wide th {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem 0.35rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    vertical-align: bottom;
  }
  .stats.wide td { padding-right: 0.6rem; vertical-align: top; }
  .stats.wide td:last-child { text-align: left; }
  .stats.wide td:first-child { white-space: nowrap; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .steps { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .steps li { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .note {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .note a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .more {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .more:hover { color: var(--muted); border-color: var(--muted); }
  .more:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ink); outline-offset: 3px; }

  /* open problems additions */
  .problem { margin-bottom: 2.2rem; }
  .problem h3 { margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .problem p { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
<div class="wrap">
  <SiteNav>
    <a class="back" href="/start/">&larr; Start here</a>
  </SiteNav>
  <article>
    <div class="meta">Open problems &middot; October 2026</div>
    <h1>Open problems: starter projects in world-model evaluation</h1>
    <p>Starter projects, from a day to a few weeks each, drawn from gaps our own work left open.
    Each links to a GitHub issue, where the details live and where you can claim it. Some will end
    in a negative result, and we publish those too. New here? Read <a href="/start/">Start here</a>
    first.</p>

    <h2>Forecasting against the market (isotherm)</h2>

    <section class="problem" id="third-forecast">
      <h3>A third forecast source for the station weather model</h3>
      <p>Does adding ECMWF's AIFS or IFS improve isotherm's station weather model at the 16:00 day-before read? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/isotherm/issues/58">issue #58</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="bitcoin-intra-hour">
      <h3>An intra-hour benchmark for Bitcoin ladders</h3>
      <p>Does free outside data carry information beyond the quote on Kalshi's hourly Bitcoin ladders, read inside the hour before close? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/isotherm/issues/59">issue #59</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="short-lead-commodities">
      <h3>A commodity model that holds up an hour before close</h3>
      <p>Can a better outside model make free futures prices competitive with Kalshi's commodity ladders 6 hours and 1 hour before close? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/isotherm/issues/60">issue #60</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="score-served-answers">
      <h3>Score the live API's answers</h3>
      <p>How good are the answers the live API actually serves? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/isotherm/issues/61">issue #61</a></p>
    </section>

    <h2>Sealed forward tests (forward)</h2>

    <section class="problem" id="spread-entries">
      <h3>Spread-aware weather entries</h3>
      <p>Would EMOS with NBM's own spread, or isotherm's station network, beat forward's best weather entry? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/forward/issues/3">issue #3</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="fine-tuned-tsfm">
      <h3>Does fine-tuning help a time-series foundation model beat copying?</h3>
      <p>Zero-shot, no released time-series foundation model beats copying the last price on Kalshi's price ladders. Does one beat it after fine-tuning on the underlyings? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/forward/issues/4">issue #4</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="forward-dry-run">
      <h3>Reproduce the price-ladder dry run from forward alone</h3>
      <p>Can a new contributor reproduce task 2 from a clone of forward? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/forward/issues/2">issue #2</a></p>
    </section>

    <h2>Probing learned representations (causal-jepa)</h2>

    <section class="problem" id="e12-convergence">
      <h3>Finish the convergence run that could reopen the programme</h3>
      <p>Does more training make the representation worse (finding 8), or was that an artefact of wide readouts? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/causal-jepa/issues/4">issue #4</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="ten-minute-vol">
      <h3>Does the one surviving lift replicate at ten minutes?</h3>
      <p>Does the training lift on future realised volatility survive the raw-feature control at a ten-minute horizon, as it does at five? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/causal-jepa/issues/5">issue #5</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="transfer-headroom">
      <h3>Headroom on a different asset class, before any training</h3>
      <p>Can the probe targets that failed on hourly crypto ladders rank representations on another asset class? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/causal-jepa/issues/6">issue #6</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="problem" id="corpus-root">
      <h3>Run the experiments on a locally rebuilt corpus</h3>
      <p>Can a contributor rebuild the corpus and run every script without extra configuration? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/causal-jepa/issues/7">issue #7</a></p>
    </section>

    <h2>Evaluating under intervention</h2>

    <section class="problem" id="intervention-task">
      <h3>Design an intervention test for world models</h3>
      <p>Can we build a small, reproducible test of whether a model's predicted outcome of an action matches what actually happens? <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/forward/issues/5">issue #5</a></p>
    </section>

    <p class="coda">Claim a problem by commenting on its issue. Propose a new one by opening an
    issue on the repository it belongs to. Contributing guides: in each repository,
    <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/isotherm">isotherm</a>,
    <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/forward">forward</a>,
    <a href="https://github.com/physicalreasoning/causal-jepa">causal-jepa</a>.
    Background: <a href="/start/">Start here</a>.</p>
  </article>
  <SiteFooter />
</div>
</Base>
